From: ios14-lithium
Subject: [build] reject unsupported per-pmap signing exceptions

The public generic ARM pmap omits pmap_cs_allow_invalid and reserves the
private code-signing fields. Without PMAP_CS, report KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED.
This does not grant W+X or silently claim that a signing exception succeeded.
Enabling a real PMAP_CS provider remains necessary for this feature.

diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
@@ -20180,7 +20180,11 @@
 vm_map_cs_wx_enable(
 	vm_map_t map)
 {
+#if PMAP_CS
 	return pmap_cs_allow_invalid(vm_map_pmap(map));
+#else
+	return KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+#endif
 }
 
 void
